// src/v4/lens/affected_set.dag
//
// Scope: affected-set lens — given a diff over the dependency graph, derive the MINIMAL subgraph that must re-execute. Canonical authority for incremental execution + CI job selection. scripts/detect-affected-components.sh is the interim BOOTSTRAP BRIDGE; this lens is the structural authority that replaces it (per feedback_no_textual_enforcement_bridges).
// Anchor: THESIS "Free consequences" §205-210 (incremental cross-run execution) + v4-close-interrogation.md §2.5.F affected-set + memory: feedback_no_textual_enforcement_bridges
// Why EARLY (operator 2026-05-15: "something i wanted to get working
//   very early on"): load-bearing for incremental execution AND it is
//   the structural replacement for the shell script currently gating
//   v2/v3/v4 CI selection. Phase 1.5.
//
// Owns:
//   - affected_set: (Dag, Diff) -> Witness<ReExecFrontier>
//     (the minimal node set that must re-run; everything else is
//     incrementally skippable because pure + unchanged)
//     (`Diff` is the std/node.dag D1 type — Path/Edit/Diff;
//      this lens CONSUMES it, it does not own it. The frontier seed is
//      the set of changed Paths; "unchanged" is `content_hash` (B1)
//      equality — the structural-caching dual already stated below.
//      The D1 OPERATION `apply_diff` lives in lens/application.dag,
//      not here: affected_set only reads the Diff, never applies it.)
//   - composes with compiler/05_eval.dag (skip unchanged pure subgraphs)
//   - composes with workflow/ci.dag (gate/job selection — replaces the
//     interim scripts/detect-affected-components.sh shell bridge)
//   - structural caching is the DUAL of the affected set — the SAME
//     mechanism, not a separate system. A build/exec artifact's cache key
//     IS `content_hash` (B1, std/node.dag) of its input subgraph: the
//     affected set names what changed (re-run); a cache restores what did
//     NOT (skip the work). Purity + content-addressing make every
//     artifact memoizable by construction (THESIS "free consequences:
//     automatic memoization") — caching is this lens read the other way.
//     ONE content-hash keys a CI artifact cache, a remote build cache, or
//     a local memo table equally; the backend (e.g. GHA `actions/cache`)
//     is just an emission target of the hash.
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/node.dag (incl. the D1 Diff type), std/witness.dag
//   - compiler/04_infer.dag: the typed dependency graph (Dag)
//
// Status: scaffold — fill per TASKS.md T-21
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md; this file's I/O contract is the immutable
// contract for the worker. Splitting this file requires explicit operator
// ratification (substrate extension = stop signal).

module v4.lens.affected_set

